Cards, Debit Cards, Credit Cards, ATMs & Mobile Wallets
9. Pre-authorizations and pending transactions
Some merchants reserve an estimated amount before the final transaction is known. This is common for:
- hotels;
- car rental companies;
- fuel stations;
- restaurants with tips;
- online orders with split shipments;
- public transport and toll systems;
- security deposits.
A pre-authorization reduces the available balance but is not always the final amount. It normally expires automatically if the merchant does not settle it. Aurora Bank can remove a hold early only if the merchant provides release confirmation or scheme rules permit release.

Payments, Transfers & Cutoff Times
7. Future-dated payments and standing orders
A future-dated payment is executed on a date chosen by the customer. A standing order is a repeated future-dated payment. The customer must ensure there is enough available balance before the payment is due.
If there is not enough available balance at the processing time, Aurora Bank may:
- reject the payment;
- retry the payment later the same day;
- create or increase an arranged overdraft if available and permitted;
- create an unarranged overdraft only where permitted by product terms.
