Payments, Transfers & Cutoff Times
7. Future-dated payments and standing orders
A future-dated payment is executed on a date chosen by the customer. A standing order is a repeated future-dated payment. The customer must ensure there is enough available balance before the payment is due.
If there is not enough available balance at the processing time, Aurora Bank may:
- reject the payment;
- retry the payment later the same day;
- create or increase an arranged overdraft if available and permitted;
- create an unarranged overdraft only where permitted by product terms.
Rejected-payment fees may apply. See [Fees, Interest & Foreign Exchange](06_fees_interest_and_exchange_rates.md).

Payments, Transfers & Cutoff Times
5. Required payment information
To make a payment, a customer must provide complete and accurate information. For SEPA transfers, this normally includes:
- beneficiary name;
- IBAN;
- amount;
- payment reference or description;
- execution date;
- optional beneficiary address for some payments.
For international wires, Aurora Bank may also require the beneficiary bank name, BIC/SWIFT code, intermediary bank information, beneficiary address, country, purpose of payment, and supporting documents.
Aurora Bank processes many payments using the account identifier provided. The beneficiary name may not always be checked by the receiving bank. Customers should verify account details before approving a payment.

Privacy, Data Protection & Open Banking
6. Sharing data
Aurora Bank may share data with:
- payment systems and card schemes;
- beneficiary and sending banks;
- credit reference agencies;
- fraud prevention agencies;
- regulators, tax authorities, courts, law enforcement, and ombudsman bodies;
- service providers such as IT hosting, card production, statement printing, call-center systems, and document verification providers;
- debt collection agencies and legal advisers where permitted;
- insurers or benefit providers for packaged accounts;
- open banking providers where the customer authorizes access;
- persons appointed by the customer, such as attorneys, guardians, executors, or authorized representatives.
We do not sell customer transaction data to advertisers.

Fees, Interest & Foreign Exchange
9. Foreign exchange rates
Foreign exchange may apply to card transactions, international transfers, cash withdrawals, refunds, and account conversions.
Aurora Bank may use:
- a card scheme wholesale rate plus Aurora Bank FX spread;
- an Aurora Bank reference exchange rate quoted before payment;
- a treasury rate for larger transfers;
- a rate provided by a third-party payment partner;
- a merchant or ATM dynamic currency conversion rate where the customer chooses it.
Rates can change continuously. The rate shown before authorization may differ from the final settlement rate for card transactions.

